[medium] internal/service/worker/dashboard_suggestion_worker.go:106 (correctness)
The rate-limit snooze budget is checked with job.Attempt, but River v0.30 explicitly does not count snoozes as attempts and the executor decrements the attempt when JobSnooze is returned. Under a persistent 429, job.Attempt never reaches maxRateLimitSnoozes, so the cell can snooze indefinitely instead of eventually failing and finalizing the run as the code comment intends.
Suggested fix: Base the snooze budget on persisted state that River does not decrement, such as the cell's rate_limited_count or River's snoozes metadata, and add a test that simulates more than maxRateLimitSnoozes repeated rate limits for the same cell and verifies it is failed/cancelled.
Guidance: In internal/service/worker/dashboard_suggestion_worker.go, stop using job.Attempt as the 429 snooze budget because River v0.30.1 decrements attempts for JobSnooze. Use the persisted dashboard_suggestion_run_cells.rate_limited_count that is already loaded with the pending cell. In Work, change the call from rateLimitSnooze(err, job.Attempt) to rateLimitSnooze(err, cell.RateLimitedCount) or a clearly named equivalent. Update rateLimitSnooze's second parameter name and comment from attempt to rateLimitedCount/snoozeCount, and keep the cap check as `if rateLimitedCount >= maxRateLimitSnoozes { return 0, false }` so the first 20 observed snoozes are allowed and the next rate limit fails the cell. Do not make incrementCellRateLimitedCount return an error or block snoozing on increment failure; the deliberate design says increment failures are logged only and do not alter snooze behavior. Update TestRateLimitSnooze in internal/service/worker/dashboard_suggestion_worker_test.go so it describes counts, not attempts. Add an integration regression in internal/service/worker/dashboard_suggestion_worker_integration_test.go that repeatedly calls Work for the same pending cell with an llm.FakeClient returning RateLimitError and a job whose Attempt stays low; assert calls while RateLimitedCount < maxRateLimitSnoozes return JobSnooze and increment the cell, then the next call returns JobCancel, marks the cell failed, and allows finalizeRunIfReady to finalize when applicable.
