[low] internal/api/handler/oscal/dashboard_suggestion_diagnostics.go:791 (correctness)
rateLimitPressureCheck returns pass with the message "No dashboard suggestion rate-limit snoozes were observed" whenever there are zero completed/failed cells, even if RateLimitedTotal is non-zero from pending cells. A newly throttled run with only pending cells and five snoozes will therefore report a passing rate_limit_pressure check while the totals already show throttling.
Suggested fix: Only use the zero-cell branch after confirming RateLimitedTotal is zero; when RateLimitedTotal is non-zero and totalCells is zero, report the snoozes accurately and warn once the existing threshold is met. Add a diagnostics summary test with only pending rate-limited cells.
Guidance: In internal/api/handler/oscal/dashboard_suggestion_diagnostics.go, fix rateLimitPressureCheck so pending-only throttling is not reported as `pass` with `No dashboard suggestion rate-limit snoozes were observed`. Split the first branch: if totals.RateLimitedTotal == 0, return the existing no-snoozes pass. If totalCells == 0 and totals.RateLimitedTotal > 0, return a message that snoozes were observed while no cells have completed or failed yet; make it `warn` when totals.RateLimitedTotal >= 5, otherwise `pass` with a below-threshold message. Only compute the ratio when totalCells > 0 to avoid division by zero. Add a summary endpoint test in internal/api/handler/oscal/dashboard_suggestions_integration_test.go that seeds only pending dashboard_suggestion_run_cells with rate_limited_count totaling at least 5, ensures loadTotals is aggregating cell-level RateLimitedTotal, and asserts the `rate_limit_pressure` check is warn instead of pass/no-snoozes.
